    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-10-21T11:21:50+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-21T11:21:50+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-21T00:51:50Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-21T00:51:50Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A trough of low pressure lingers about the east, before weakening later today, as a slow moving high pressure system in the Tasman Sea will re-establish a ridge across southern parts. A trough is then forecast to briefly move into the west on Thursday, before another trough and cold front move more broadly across SA on Friday and Saturday.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW014" description="North East Pastoral" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-10-21T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-22T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-20T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-21T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Slight chance of a shower north of Oodnadatta, near zero chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm. Winds east to southeasterly 15 to 20 km/h tending south to southeasterly 20 to 30 km/h in the middle of the day then tending east to southeasterly 15 to 25 km/h in the late evening. Daytime maximum temperatures 29 to 38.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">Moderate</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:10am to 4:40pm, UV Index predicted to reach 10 [Very High]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-10-22T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-23T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-21T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-22T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. The chance of fog south of Yunta in the early morning. Medium chance of showers north of Leigh Creek, near zero chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm north of Leigh Creek in the afternoon and evening. Winds east to northeasterly 20 to 30 km/h tending north to northeasterly 15 to 20 km/h in the middle of the day then tending northeast to southeasterly 15 to 25 km/h in the early afternoon. Overnight temperatures falling to between 16 and 24 with daytime temperatures reaching the low to mid 30s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-10-23T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-24T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-22T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-23T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Slight chance of a shower north of Leigh Creek in the morning. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm in the morning and afternoon. Winds northeast to southeasterly 15 to 25 km/h tending northwest to northeasterly during the morning then tending northeast to southeasterly 15 to 20 km/h during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 18 and 22 with daytime temperatures reaching the low to mid 30s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-10-24T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-25T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-23T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-24T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Medium chance of showers, most likely in the afternoon and evening. The chance of a thunderstorm. Winds north to northeasterly 15 to 25 km/h tending north to northwesterly during the day then tending southeast to southwesterly 20 to 30 km/h during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 18 and 23 with daytime temperatures reaching 33 to 38.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
